ated by SDS-PAGE, and the separated proteins were transferred to NC membranes and blocked with 5% skim milk for 2 h. Primary antibodies (NLRP3, ASC, GSDMD-N, pro-caspase-1, cleaved caspase-1 p20, and pro-IL-1β) were incubated overnight at 4 ℃ with slow shaking. Secondary antibodies were incubated at room temperature for 2 h. The images were developed with an ultrasensitive multifunctional chemiluminescence image. The gray values in Western blot bands were quantified using ImageJ software. Observation of the microscopic morphological characteristics of pyroptosis The experimental group was the same as the (B) same-viability group. When the incubation time was reached, the cells were washed twice with PBS, and the cell morphology was observed under a fluorescent microscope. Subsequently, cells were fixed with electron microscope fixative overnight at 4 ℃ and washed three times with PBS. The cells were dehydrated with gradient concentrations of ethanol (25%, 50%, 70%, 90%, and 100%), subjected to critical point drying with CO 2 , and sprayed with gold. Their morphology was observed by SEM. Pyroptosis observed by PI staining The experimental group was the same as the (B) same-viability group. After the incubation time, the cells were washed twice with PBS. The cells were incubated in PI working solution for 30 min at 4 ℃ and washed twice with PBS. The cells were observed under a fluorescent microscope. Casepase-1/propidium iodide (PI) double staining quantitative analysis The experimental group was the same as the (B) same-viability group. The green fluorescence probe FAM-YVAD-FMK was used to label caspase-1 in living cells [ 29 ]. After treatment, the cells were incubated at 37 ℃ in the dark for 1 h with FAM-YVAD-FMK solution, washed twice with the wash solution provided by the FLICA caspase-1 detection kit, and incubated at room temperature in the dark for 10 min with PI staining solution. Cell population was detected by flow cytometry. Characteristics of pyroptosis observed by caspase-1/PI/Hoechst 33342 triple staining The experimental group was the same as the (B) same-viability group. Cells were seeded in 3.5 mm confocal dishes. After the incubation time, the cells were washed twice with PBS and stained with FAM-YVAD-FMK solution for 1 h. The staining solution was removed, and the cells were washed three times with PBS. About 300 μL of Hoechst 33342 working solution (10 μg/mL) was added and stained for 10 min. The staining solution was removed, and the cells were washed three times with PBS. Subsequently, 300 μL of PI working solution (10 μg/mL) was added and stained for 10 min. The staining solution was removed by aspiration, and the cells were washed with PBS for three times and observed under laser confocal microscopy. ELISA was used to detect the release of IL-1β and IL-18 The experimental group was the same as the (B) same-viability group. Cells were seeded in 6-well plates. After the incubation time, the cells were washed twice with PBS and operated according to the instructions of the IL-1β ELISA kit and IL-18 ELISA kit. Observation of cell polarization Observation of microscopic morphological characteristics of cell polarization The experimental group was the same as the (B) same-viability group. SEM samples were prepared as in Sect. “ Observation of the microscopic morphological characteristics of pyroptosis ”. Qualitative analysis of cell polarization The experimental group was the same as the (B) same-viability group. Cells were seeded in 3.5 mm confocal dishes. After the incubation time, the cells were washed twice with PBS. The cells were fixed using 4% paraformaldehyde fixative for 15 min and washed three times with PBS. After fixation, the cells were permeabilized (only in the detection of iNOS) for 10 min and washed three times with PBS. The cells were incubated with CD86/iNOS/CD163/CD206 primary antibodies overnight at 4 ℃ and secondary antibodies for 1 h at room temperature, followed by 300 μL of DAPI staining for 8 min. The staining solution was removed, and the cells were washed three times with PBS and observed by laser confocal microscopy. Quantitative analysis of cell polarization The experimental group was the same as the (B) same-viability group. Cells were seeded in 6-well plates. When the incubation time was reached, the cells were fixed with 4% paraformaldehyde and incubated overnight at 4 ℃ with CD86 or CD206 primary antibodies, followed by incubation for 1 h at room temperature with secondary antibodies. The staining solution was removed, and the cells were washed three times with PBS. The cells were collected, and the cell population was detected by flow cytometry. Zeta potential of COM crystal Zeta potentials of COM crystals of different sizes were examined. In this work, 3 mg of COM crystals was weighed and dispersed in 6 mL of ethyl alcohol or RPMI-1640 culture medium. The zeta potential of the samples was determined using a Zetasizer Nano ZS laser nanoparticle size analyzer. Statistical analysis Data are presented as means ± SD. The number of individual experiments is indicated in the Figures or figure legends. One-way ANOVA was used for statistical analysis by SPSS 13.0 software. In all Figures, significance was defined as follows: *P < 0.05, **P < 0.01, ***P < 0.001. P ≥ 0.05 were considered not significant.

